From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 12/23] drm/mediatek, soc: mediatek, pwm: power the display down; SODI requests; drm/panel: add the Synaptics R63308 panel

mediatek-drm removes a firmware framebuffer (the bootloader's, through
simplefb) before registering. The MT6771's DSI interrupt is requested
before the host registers. panel-synaptics-r63308 drives the Titan
Pocket's 720x720 MIPI-DSI panel with the vendor's power and init
sequences.

The display's power domain now goes off with the CRTC: AAL, CCORR,
COLOR, GAMMA, the DSI, the mutex and the display PWM gain runtime PM
(genpd counted them as in use), each holding the domain while it is
clocked or powered; the display PWM switches off at duty 0, which
pwm-backlight asks for with the backlight off. For the SPM's SODI, as
MediaTek's display does for a video-mode panel: mmsys sets the MT6771's
SODI request mask while the path runs (RDMA0's AP-source request held,
DDREN from its FIFO), and RDMA0 gets its SODI FIFO thresholds.
